  "notes": "Extracted from the primary paper (snippet: The M9+glucose minimal medium definition includes less restrictive uptake rates and fewer nutrient sources. It is simulated with unlimited uptake rates for Calcium, Chloride, CO2, Co2+, Cu2+, Fe2+, Fe). Component names mapped to BiGG (see mapping_confidence); presence-based bounds unless the paper gave exchange bounds; concentration_mM where units allowed. Extraction confidence: medium.",
  "verification": "paper-verified (corrected via workflow)",
  "base_expansion": "Base 'M9' expanded to standard composition: M9 minimal medium (Sambrook & Russell 2001): Na2HPO4, KH2PO4, NaCl, NH4Cl, MgSO4, CaCl2 + carbon source.",
  "verification_evidence": "The M9+glucose minimal medium definition includes less restrictive uptake rates and fewer nutrient sources. It is simulated with unlimited uptake rates for Calcium, Chloride, CO2, Co2+, Cu2+, Fe2+, Fe3+, Potassium, Magnesium, Mn2+, Molybdate, Sodium, Ammonium, Phosphate, Sulfate, Tungstate, and Zinc and limited uptake rates for 2,3 Di-hydroxybenzoate, O2, H+, H2O, D-Glucose, and Cob(1)alamin",
  "verification_confidence": "high",
